# Cloudflare Pages' own default for plain files (no build step, no
# content-hashed filenames — every page here is a static file with an
# inline <script>, per CLAUDE.md's own "no shared build system" note)
# caches .js/.css for 4 hours (`max-age=14400`). Confirmed live, 10 Sep
# 2026, as a real, recurring source of confusion: a citizen (or this
# session's own testing) could load a page, have its shared script
# (digest.js, builder.html's own logic, civics.js, mode.js) cached for
# up to 4 hours, and see zero visible effect from a real fix shipped and
# deployed in the meantime — reading as "the fix didn't actually work"
# when it was purely a stale cache. `no-cache` doesn't mean "never
# cache" — it means "always revalidate with the server first," which,
# combined with the ETag Cloudflare already sends, is cheap (a tiny 304
# when nothing changed) while guaranteeing a real change reaches the
# browser on the very next load instead of up to 4 hours later.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
